.cards {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 1rem;
}
.card {
  flex: 1 1 100%; /* full width on mobile */
}

@media (min-width: 600px) {
  .card { flex: 1 1 calc(50% - 1rem); } /* 2 columns */
}
@media (min-width: 900px) {
  .card { flex: 1 1 calc(33.33% - 1rem); } /* 3 columns */
}

slides.content:
# No Media Queries Needed

CSS Grid with `auto-fit` and `minmax()` can create fully responsive grids without any breakpoints:
```css
.gallery {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
}
```
The browser adds as many 250px+ columns as fit, and `1fr` makes them expand equally. Perfect for card layouts, galleries, or product grids.

slides.codeSnippet:
.layout {
  display: grid;
  gap: 20px;
}
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .layout {
    grid-template-columns: 250px 1fr;
    grid-template-areas: "sidebar main";
  }
  .sidebar { grid-area: sidebar; }
  .main-content { grid-area: main; }
}

slides.content:
# Beyond Viewport‑Based Breakpoints

Container queries allow you to style elements based on the size of their parent container, not the whole viewport. They're now widely supported (2023+).

```css
.card-container {
  container-type: inline-size;
}
@container (min-width: 400px) {
  .card {
    display: flex;
  }
}
```
This makes components truly reusable, adapting to wherever they're placed.
